# API_ENTITIES.md was split per resource, so the moved section titles are the
# bare words People / Organizations / Roles / Assignments / Jurisdictions /
# Entity Events. check-seams then flags every line in the surface containing
# one of those words — 205 hits, e.g. an admin breadcrumb (<a>Organizations</a>)
# and a scope-table row. Verified none is real: `grep -rn "API_ENTITIES.md §"`
# returns nothing, and the only two inbound references (the AGENTS.md index and
# PUBLIC_API.md:7) name the file, never a section.
# NOT acked on purpose. An ack entry must be a contiguous substring of
# "<class> <path> <line>", so the only entry that would match here is the
# blanket "moved-title" — which would also silence increments 3-6 of #428,
# where the check still has to work. The count is carried on the ledger row
# instead, and the heuristic is filed upstream: a one-word section title should
# require a doc reference alongside it, not match the word alone.

